    "result_text": "The full suite is green. There's a single test class (`AcceptanceTest`) and it passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the customerCode de-duplication rule in `OwnerRestControllerV1.customerCode(Owner)`:\n\n- The base code is still computed as `<REGION>-<HASH8>`.\n- I now collect the `customerCode` of all existing owners and, if the base code already collides, append `-<n>` starting at `n = 2`, incrementing until the value is unique (`NSW-1A2B3C4D-2`, `-3`, \u2026).\n- If there's no collision, the base code is returned unchanged.\n\nThis runs before `membershipNumber(...)` is derived, so the membership number correctly builds on the de-duplicated code. The `coreCustomerCodesStayUnique` acceptance test and the full suite (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`) pass \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
